<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $g^{\ast }: \calX ^{/S} \rightarrow \calX ^{/S'}$ be a pullback functor. Without loss of generality we may suppose that $f' = g^{\ast } f$. Let $U_{\bullet }: \Nerve (\cDelta _{+})^{op} \rightarrow \calX $ be a Čech nerve of $f$. Since $g^{\ast }$ is left exact (being a right adjoint), we conclude that $g^{\ast } \circ U_{\bullet }$ is a Čech nerve of $f'$. If $f$ is an effective epimorphism, then $U_{\bullet }$ is a colimit diagram. Because colimits in $\calX $ are universal, $g^{\ast } \circ U_{\bullet }$ is also a colimit diagram, so that $f'$ is an effective epimorphism. 
    <p>
      Conversely, suppose that $f'$ and $g$ are effective epimorphisms. Corollary <a href="/tag/B75892" data-tag="B75892">6.2.3.12</a> implies that $g \circ f'$ is an effective epimorphism. The commutativity of the diagram implies that $f \circ g'$ is an effective epimorphism, so that $f$ is an effective epimorphism (Corollary <a href="/tag/B75892" data-tag="B75892">6.2.3.12</a> again). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
